aceMember is the declared handler entry.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"other-identity","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler obtains the current user and resolves the target user together with caller and target memberships.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":741,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"other-resource","kind":"binding","statement":"Target resolution requires a resolved space, a normal target user, and an active target membership.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"other-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The handler defines self-targeting by comparing targetUser.ID with currentUser.ID; the supplied other-member premise makes this comparison false.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":750,"endLine":752}]},{"id":"other-control","kind":"control","statement":"For a non-self target, the handler requires the caller membership to have the administrator role.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":751,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"other-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"Only after authorization does the handler invoke Store.DeleteSpaceMember for the target membership and publish the space change.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":756,"endLine":763}]},{"id":"other-active-role","kind":"condition","statement":"The source defines active membership as administrator or ordinary user role.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-b6a6c6968b02e733","startLine":64,"endLine":66}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]},{"obligationId":"scenario%3Aself-leave::entry%3Adelete-member","decision":{"kind":"observed","observed":"allow"},"branchResults":[],"explanation":"At the declared DeleteSpaceMember entry, the source first requires an authenticated current user and resolves the caller's and target's active memberships. The handler compares targetUser.ID with currentUser.ID; under the accepted self-leave premise, isSelf is true, so the non-self administrator check is skipped. The handler then reaches the protected Store.DeleteSpaceMember effect and publishes the change, subject to any returned mutation error. Source-visible authorization is therefore allow. Separately, this matches the accepted original policy, which allows an active space member to delete their own membership without administrator authority. This assesses only the declared entry and supplied source; repository completeness and deployment behavior remain untested.","facts":[{"id":"self-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the declared handler entry.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"self-identity","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler obtains the current user and resolves the target user together with caller and target memberships.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":741,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"self-resource","kind":"binding","statement":"Target resolution requires a resolved space, a normal target user, and an active target membership.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"self-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The handler defines self-targeting by comparing targetUser.ID with currentUser.ID; the supplied self-leave premise makes this comparison true.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":750,"endLine":751}]},{"id":"self-control","kind":"control","statement":"The administrator check is guarded by the non-self condition, so it is not applied when the target is the caller.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":750,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"self-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"The handler invokes Store.DeleteSpaceMember for the resolved target membership and publishes the space change after the call succeeds.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":756,"endLine":763}]},{"id":"self-active-role","kind":"condition","statement":"The source defines active membership as administrator or ordinary user role.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-b6a6c6968b02e733","startLine":64,"endLine":66}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]}]}}],"tokens":{"input":4879,"output":1425,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":68760.07080000002,"stopReason":"tool_use"},"schemaValidation":{"valid":true,"diagnostics":[]},"endedAt":"2026-09-29T08:19:34.191Z"}}
